      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ICED POPPY (3) has the right blend of current form and proven partnership to be the horse to beat. She was beaten half a length at Cranbourne after travelling well and fighting on, and that followed a second in a FM BM70 at Pakenham Synthetic, so her consistency stands out. Lachlan King has won three from nine on her and sets up for every hope. TENNESSEE SONG (8) resumes from a five-month break with three trials behind her and has stronger mid-week and  BM70 form than a plain heavy-track sixth at Sandown-Lakeside suggests. SYNCHRO (1) drops back from Saturday BM70 company, was held up near the 200m when beaten two lengths at Morphettville, and the apprentice claim gives him a sound place platform despite the 1200m query. YOOMEE WONDER (5) was good late last start and has to be included in the small field.",
